le></div><p><em>&ldquo;Not advertised&rdquo; means we couldn't find the feature on the product's own pages. It may still exist; check the listing.</em></p></article></div></section>
 <section><div class="wrap feature-blocks"><article class="feature-block"><h2>Each option in one paragraph</h2><h3 id="sheetspeed">1. SheetSpeed</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> Analysts and modelers who want free formula tracing plus Excel-style shortcuts in Google Sheets and Slides.</p><p>We make SheetSpeed. Trace precedents (Ctrl+Shift+[) is free in Core, with Excel-style Alt sequences and Slides shortcuts. No ads or tracking inside the extension. <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/ljlmgielacploapelnjhodicgbjipcaa" rel="noopener">Chrome Web Store page</a>.</p><h3 id="sheetwhiz">2. SheetWhiz</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> Finance teams that want the most-installed option and a long track record (since 2023).</p><p>Pro adds trace precedents/dependents, goal seek, what-if/data sensitivities, paste special, auto-color and format/font/fill cycles. <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/bfncmfmdadhimlnpeecppaimgmeeppan" rel="noopener">Chrome Web Store page</a>.</p><h3 id="shortiecuts">3. ShortieCuts</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> People who want the widest Office Alt-key coverage with an on-screen Key Tips overlay, including Word shortcuts in Google Docs.</p><p>Also has Accumulate, chart format presets, F4 repeat, Ctrl+9/0 hide. Its privacy page says it logs shortcut names with Google Analytics. <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/jbhdbmffapbbghcejohkekfecihgehlc" rel="noopener">Chrome Web Store page</a>.</p><h3 id="spex">4. Spex</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> People who want visual on-screen KeyTips and can choose between Excel-style and Sheets-style workflows.</p><p>Young, actively updated project; Quick Access and dark mode. <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/gahnolkboklnjhnaahjdkingoejbepcc" rel="noopener">Chrome Web Store page</a>.</p><h3 id="xlkeys">5. XLKeys</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> Currently unavailable (checked Oct 18, 2026).</p><p>Currently unavailable (checked Oct 18, 2026). On that date xlkeyz.com returned a 503 deployment pause and its Chrome Web Store listing said not available. We are not saying it shut down. <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/jpdneiofokgelbncbjcknpclmgpekllc" rel="noopener">Chrome Web Store page</a>.</p><h3 id="google-sheets-built-in-toggle">6. Google Sheets built-in toggle</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> Anyone who only needs common Ctrl shortcuts and can&#x27;t install extensions.</p><p>Covers many Ctrl shortcuts, but no Alt ribbon sequences (Alt H O I, Alt E S V) and no formula tracing. <a href="https://support.google.com/docs/answer/181110" rel="noopener">Google help page</a>.</p></article></div></section>
-<section><div class="wrap feature-blocks"><article class="feature-block"><h2>How to choose</h2><ul><li><strong>Only need common Ctrl shortcuts, or can't install extensions:</strong> turn on Google's compatible spreadsheet shortcuts first. <a href="/blog/how-to-enable-excel-shortcuts-in-google-sheets/">How to enable it</a>.</li><li><strong>Financial modeling on a budget (tracing, goal seek, what-if):</strong> SheetSpeed (tracing is free) or SheetWhiz Pro.</li><li><strong>The most-installed option:</strong> SheetWhiz.</li><li><strong>Widest Alt-key coverage with an on-screen overlay, plus Docs:</strong> ShortieCuts.</li><li><strong>Visual KeyTips in Sheets only:</strong> Spex.</li><li><strong>Work laptop:</strong> ask IT to allowlist the extension by its Chrome Web Store id (SheetSpeed: ljlmgielacploapelnjhodicgbjipcaa) and check each product's permissions before installing.</li></ul><p>Head-to-head pages: <a href="/blog/sheetwhiz-alternative/">SheetSpeed vs SheetWhiz</a> · <a href="/blog/sheetspeed-vs-shortiecuts/">SheetSpeed vs ShortieCuts</a> · <a href="/blog/sheetspeed-vs-spex/">SheetSpeed vs Spex</a> · <a href="/blog/sheetspeed-vs-xlkeys/">SheetSpeed vs XLKeys</a>. Reference: <a href="/blog/google-sheets-shortcuts-list/">Google Sheets shortcuts list (Windows, Mac, Excel equivalents)</a> · <a href="/blog/excel-shortcuts-in-google-sheets-guide/">complete guide to Excel shortcuts in Google Sheets</a>.</p><p><a class="nav-cta" href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/ljlmgielacploapelnjhodicgbjipcaa" rel="noopener" data-store-cta>Add SheetSpeed to Chrome (free)</a></p></article></div></section>
